le_source":"cdsl/wil/wilheader.xml (TEI teiHeader)"},{"i":50,"code":"yat","name":"Yates's Dictionary in Sanscrit and English","name_from":"TEI teiHeader","title":"Yates's Dictionary in Sanscrit and English","author":"Thomas Malten","label":"Yates, Sanskrit-English Dictionary","year":1846,"tier":"K3","genre":"bilingual_out","domain":null,"provider":"cdsl","words":44719,"caveat":null,"rank":6,"muted":false,"title_source":"cdsl/yat/yatheader.xml (TEI teiHeader)"}],"display_order":{"schema_version":1,"purpose":"The order sources appear in a word entry, and the name each is shown under. Per the build spec of 2026-08-24, ordering and inclusion of sources belong to the project owner alone — so this file exists to be edited by him, and the code reads it rather than deciding anything.","how_to_edit":"Move a code between the tiers below to change where it appears. `rank` orders the tiers; inside a tier, sources appear in the order listed. Any indexed kośa not named here falls into the `remaining` tier automatically, so nothing is ever silently dropped by editing this file.","name_authority":"A source is shown under its TEI teiHeader title where one exists (all 44 CDSL dictionaries). The 19 indic-dict builds ship LICENSE.xml rather than a TEI header, so they fall back to the `label` recorded in rudha_sources.json. NEITHER is hand-typed here. Where `display_name` appears below it is a correction the project owner has asked for, and it wins over both.","outstanding":"The 19 indic-dict sources have no TEI-authoritative title and are shown under a transliterated registry label (\"Amarakosa (ontology build)\"). If proper diacritical titles are wanted, they need to come from the printed editions — they are not in the data we hold, and must not be invented here.","tiers":[{"rank":1,"key":"shrauta","label":"Śrauta padārtha","note":"Spec §2.1. Skipped silently when the word has no entry — no placeholder.","codes":["spn"]},{"rank":2,"key":"vaidika","label":"Veda references","note":"Spec §2.2. NOTE: true Veda Bhāṣya is not in the corpus yet. What sits here today is padapāṭha occurrence — where the word actually appears in the Veda, with svara. The bhāṣya layer (the 2020 Bhāṣya Pilot) has not been ingested. Rendered by the V segment, not by a kośa code.","codes":[]},{"rank":3,"key":"amarakosha","label":"Amarakośa","note":"Spec §2.3.","codes":["amara-onto","amara-sudhA"]},{"rank":4,"key":"vacaspatyam","label":"Vācaspatyam","note":"Spec §2.4. `vcp` is the CDSL digitisation and carries printed pages; the indic-dict build is a cross-check.","codes":["vcp","vAchaspatyam-sa"]},{"rank":5,"key":"shabdakalpadruma","label":"Śabdakalpadrumaḥ","note":"Spec §2.5.","codes":["skd","kalpadruma-sa"]},{"rank":6,"key":"remaining","label":"Other kośas","note":"Spec §2.6. Every indexed kośa not named in another tier lands here automatically, ordered by how many of the word's other witnesses agree with it. Nothing needs adding here by hand.","codes":[]},{"rank":7,"key":"monier_williams","label":"Monier-Williams","note":"Spec §2.7. Always last and visually de-emphasised. mw72 is the 1872 edition and rides with it.","muted":true,"codes":["mw","mw72"]}],"primary_shown":5,"primary_shown_note":"How many sources render in full before the rest collapse into 'also in: X · Y · +N more'. Spec §2 says 4–6.","display_name":{"amara-onto":"Amarakośa — ontology build","amara-sudhA":"Amarakośa with the Sudhā commentary","vAchaspatyam-sa":"Vācaspatyam — StarDict build","kalpadruma-sa":"Śabdakalpadrumaḥ — StarDict build","spn":"Śrautapadārthanirvacanam"},"display_name_note":"Only these five are corrected here, because their registry labels are ASCII transliterations of titles whose correct Devanagari-derived spelling is not in dispute. Every other source keeps its TEI title verbatim."},"vaidika_texts":[{"i":0,"code":"RV","title":"Ṛgveda Padapāṭha, maṇḍalas 1–4","veda":"rigveda","padas":79431},{"i":1,"code":"RV","title":"Ṛgveda Padapāṭha, maṇḍalas 5–8","veda":"rigveda","padas":79890},{"i":