, not the whole yaugika space.","The inflected-form layer, the only place the sūtra chain itself is shown, is still a 40-dhātu sample of 2,229.","The four-school stem analysis of manual §5 ships School A only. Schools B (Nirukta), C (Sthaulāṣṭhīvi) and D (Śākapūṇi) have no data behind them yet.","Manual §6 grammarian philosophy, §7 vivakṣā flags and §9 coinage engine are not built. They are shown as planned, never as empty features.","A render gate withholds keys that are not SLP1-clean (a locus or catalogue numeral that leaked into a headword) and keys whose Devanagari cannot be written without loss — hyphen-compound padapāṭha rows whose sandhi was never resolved. They are counted on the Corpus tab, not silently dropped."]}